^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-27 12:30] observe — Cache audit found three defects; the eviction leak is demonstrated by probe, not inferred. Document is deleted from documents; its annotation index entry survives.
 >>[2026-07-27 12:30] observe — cache.spw already specifies composite keys, hash-prefix eviction, and coupling cascade. None are implemented. The spec is a better design than what runs; treat drift as the bug.
 >>[2026-07-27 12:35] decide — Key granules on appositions rather than minting a new anchor. 220 are already placed, they are author-maintained, and the raw-body lexing makes them verifiable without a parse.
 >>[2026-07-27 12:35] taste — server-index.ts at 1234 lines is already double the guard. Granule, validity, and inbound-index logic go to packages/spw-lsp/src/cache/; server-index.ts should end this plan net smaller.
 >>[2026-07-27 12:40] observe — Coverage is the honest constraint: 182 of 493 surfaces carry an apposition. The other 63% fall back to whole-file invalidation, so the fallback path must not regress.
 >>[2026-07-27 12:40] decide — Deferred incremental parsing. LexerState is already a serializable checkpoint and both tokenize and seedNode are generators, so the affordance is real, but safe-restart-point analysis is its own plan.
 >>[2026-07-27 13:10] observe — plan-ecology sweep: granule_key is declared in .spw/patterns/surface-identity.spw alongside content_hash and shape_fingerprint. The ?[granule_agreement] question now has a surface to be answered on.
 >>[2026-08-24 12:59] revise — progressive source horizons and corpus spread are separate cache axes: editor granules key on content plus structural ancestry and profile/product revisions, while corpus tools may project a valid far/high-resolution result toward a nearer question.
 >>[2026-08-24 13:00] decide — line offsets remain locations rather than identities, and cache warmth or edit cadence never becomes a person-level or authority-facing score.
 >>[2026-09-30 16:54] revise — the leak test may proceed. The granule key waits on syntax-hardware-alignment: an apposition is not a cache convenience until it is one wire. Warmth stays off any authority-facing score.
 >>[2026-10-03 02:39] implement — Applied uncommitted (caches-cut-2026-09-30 lens patch, reviewed approve-with-nits in three rounds). WIRE: the LSP index adds an apposition kind with body; workspace/symbol matches readings on their body and ranks exact name matches first under the 40 cap; hover adds wonder and apposition cards with lens precedence apposition, datum, comment; inlay and semantic tokens paint apposition bodies as one string; spw/annotations records carry kind apposition and body; the VS Code concepts and workspace trees accept the kind. New modules packages/spw-lsp/src/apposition.ts and handlers/wonder.ts. COST: per-request medians under load (main to patched): wonder hover 0.15 to 0.92 ms, inlay 0.28 to 0.32 ms, semantic tokens on a big doc 5.0 to 6.8 ms, workspace symbol lens 10.5 to 15 ms; tests LSP 263 pass plus 1 known failure, VS Code 14 of 14, extension tsc clean. Follow-ups: spw-probes resonance, references, rename, and documentHighlight still read ~#lens( by regex.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:29] revise — Resolved ?[ordering]: spw-beat-diff-precipitation is stranded and server-index.ts still has static WARM_TTL and COLD_TTL, so no dynamic-TTL edit collides with commits 3 to 5 today.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:29] revise — Resolved ?[granule_agreement] for now: geometric-analysis-tooling is dormant and its card says not to ship a fingerprint product from character scans, so no second key format competes; reopen if it reheats.
 >>[2026-10-12 14:29] observe — Commit 6 landed in effect as b8a6949d: scanAppositions in apposition-scan.ts returns name, raw body, span and a body mask hash without a parse. The eviction leak is unfixed on reading: evictStale deletes only documents entries and no leak test exists; no peekDocument exists; server-index.ts is 1302 lines.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:36] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 2 landed, 9 planned, 0 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:39] observe — Owner screenshot, 2026-10-13: VS Code shows caches-cut-2026-09-30/wip.spw with 2 incoming file refs from .tmp/headplans and release/wt-pre copies, though neither directory exists on disk and server-index.ts skips release. Index entries outlive their documents and their directories: evidence for ~[pin_cache_defects]. caches-living-tree's journal backlinks are only as true as this eviction.
}

